SUMMARY:Fused Glass: Fall Scene Plate Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Design and create a beautiful fall-themed glass plate!\nCool crisp air? Colourful leaves? Think fall. Capture the fall colours in this fused glass class. Using Glassline Paint\, coloured frit\, and stringers\, Millean Kung will guide you through creating your own fall scene on a 6” x 6” plate. You will learn about the various types of glass\, tools involved\, and techniques used.\n \nAll materials will be provided. This course welcomes beginners.\n \nPlease note: Participants’ creations will be fired off-site and will be ready for pick up in about 4 – 6 weeks.\n \nSaturday\, September 19\, 1 to 3 p.m.\nPublic $115\, TBG Members $110 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Millean Kung\nBorn and raised in Toronto\, Millean discovered pottery and glass art more than 10 years ago. Currently\, she is a member of the of the Potter’s Studios in Scarborough and is involved in the Small Business Arts Mentorship Program at Glasstronomy Studios in Markham. Since retiring from education\, Millean has devoted her time to her pottery and glass art. She is the sole proprietor of her business\, “1 in a Millean”\, and participates in a number of arts and crafts shows.\n \nMillean also loves to garden and is a member and a volunteer at the Toronto Botanical Garden. To keep her schedule busy\, she enjoys cooking and baking.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/fused-glass-fall-scene-plate-workshop/
