SUMMARY:Autumn Succulent Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us this autumn season and create a one-of-a-kind succulent arrangement!\nEmbrace the beauty of the autumn season with our hands-on succulent arranging workshop. In this cozy and creative session\, you’ll craft a stunning succulent arrangement in a handmade terracotta bowl planter\, perfect for adding warmth and charm to your fall décor.\n \nGuided by an expert succulent designer\, you’ll learn the art of arranging succulents with seasonal flair\, incorporating tips on plant care and design techniques to create a balanced and vibrant display. The terracotta bowl\, with its natural earthy tones\, makes a perfect canvas for your living masterpiece.\n \nAll materials are provided\, including a variety of premium succulents\, specialty soil\, and care instruction cards to keep your arrangement thriving through the season and beyond.\n \nCapture the essence of autumn with this delightful workshop and leave with a unique creation to celebrate nature’s colours and textures. Whether for your home or as a gift\, this arrangement is sure to impress!\n \nThursday\, October 1\, 7 to 8 p.m.\nPublic $60\, TBG Members $55 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Canadian Succulents\nMolly is the owner and operator of the small business Canadian Succulents. Canadian Succulents creates floral arrangements using only succulents and cacti plants. They not only arrange and design all of the creations\, but also grow all the plants that can be found in them as well. The business operates out of a greenhouse northeast of the city\, where over 300 varieties of succulents and cacti are grown. Molly grows and creates these designs for wedding centrepieces and favours\, corporate events and gifting\, and hotel and office greenery.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
