SUMMARY:Paper Quilling: Fall Tree Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the magic of autumn with a relaxing day of creativity at the beautiful Toronto Botanical Garden!\nJoin artist Deepa Krishnan for a fun\, beginner-friendly paper quilling workshop. In this 4-hour session\, you’ll learn a variety of quilling techniques while creating a stunning fall tree on an 8”x10” canvas. Inspired by the rich colours of the season\, you’ll have the freedom to choose your own autumn palette\, making your artwork truly one of a kind.\n \nThis workshop includes a 30-minute lunch break. We recommend bringing your own lunch to enjoy while taking in the beautiful surroundings of the garden.\n \nWhether you’re trying paper quilling for the first time or looking to expand your skills\, this workshop is a wonderful way to slow down\, get creative\, and celebrate the beauty of the season.\n \nAll supplies are included\, and no prior experience needed. This workshop is suitable for adults and children ages 12 and above.\n \nSunday\, October 18\, 10:30 a.m. to 3 p.m.\nPublic $100\, TBG Members $90 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Deepa Krishnan\nDeepa Krishnan is a self-taught artist specializing in the art of paper quilling\, which involves manipulating narrow strips of paper to create exquisite designs. She discovered this art form when she was looking for a creative outlet from her engineering job. She was amazed by the possibilities and beauty of paper quilling\, that she decided to pursue it as a full-time career. Since then\, she has been passionately mastering this technique and has created many artworks drawing inspiration from nature\, music and travel. She cuts the paper strips in different widths to add depth and dimension to her creations. She loves to play with the colours and experiment with the quilling techniques to create her own distinctive style. Deepa believes that anyone can learn this art form\, regardless of their age or skill level\, and she hosts many workshops to spread the joy of quilling. She enjoys seeing her students discover their own creativity and style in paper quilling.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/paper-quilling-fall-tree-workshop/
